title: "MicroLens: Microscopy Vision-Language Model"
authors:
  - family-names: Brinza
    given-names: Serghei
    affiliation: Independent Researcher, Vienna, Austria
date-released: 2026-05-17
version: "Final-1.0"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/SergheiBrinza/microlens"
url: "https://huggingface.co/Laborator/microlens-final"
abstract: "Fine-tuned Gemma 4 E2B vision-language model for offline biological microscopy. Trained on 75,491 image-question-answer pairs spanning 95 genera of diatoms and fungal spores from three license-clean source datasets (UDE Diatoms CC0, DIATLAS CC-BY 4.0, TgFC CC-BY 4.0). Built for the Kaggle Gemma 4 Good Hackathon 2026."
keywords:
  - gemma-4
  - microscopy
  - vision-language-model
  - unsloth
  - on-device-ai
  - diatoms
  - fungal-spores
